{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791548770,"nonce":"vL0ALOgJsZ+el/eTSzY1pICr0mw=","title":"Array.iterator erases its element type before monomorphization","message":"At 94d14e941e8ad43a221f4996caa1ffe5639e60f8, infer_builtin_method_type returns Dynamic for Array\u003cT\u003e.iterator() and keyValueIterator(). GenericArrayIteration first\u003cT\u003e(values:Array\u003cT\u003e) then loses the next() result type; the generic body can select an ambiguous runtime method or a same-named method instead of ArrayIterator.next. Calls accepting Iterator\u003cT\u003e also cannot infer T from ArrayIterator\u003cT\u003e because structural class-method signatures are compared without substituting the receiver's arguments.\n\nPreserve ArrayIterator\u003cT\u003e and ArrayKeyValueIterator\u003cT\u003e as the declared return types. Substitute class-method types when inferring structural arguments. Route the built-in ArrayIterator's calls and protocol-handle entries through its MIR slot wrappers, and preserve a generic next result's TypeVar conversion for the monomorphizer. A concrete ArrayIterator\u003cDynamic\u003e supplies the boxed-slot element type explicitly. GenericArrayIteration covers generic returns, forwarded generic calls, Iterator\u003cT\u003e parameters, Float constraints, Dynamic slots and nested arrays. Reproductions and monomorphization diagnostics are in /tmp/rayzor-generic-array-iteration-pinned-v4.log, /tmp/rayzor-generic-array-iteration-renamed-v4.log and /tmp/rayzor-generic-array-iteration-pinned-v5.log. Full validation pending.","files":null}]}